course: dictionary
lesson: 5190
title: One word, many jackets
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word jacket has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one you need. «He put on his jacket because the wind was cold.» Here a jacket is a short coat with sleeves that you wear over your other clothes.
explain: «The book jacket showed a dragon on the front.» Here jacket means a cover that wraps around something. Ask yourself: what is being covered? The clue is the word book.
explain: «Put on your life jacket before you get in the kayak.» Life and kayak are the clues. A life jacket is a vest that keeps you floating in water, so it is for safety, not for warmth.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "Put on your coat before you get in the kayak" does not quite fit, so the water clue points to a life jacket.
fact: A jacket is a short coat with sleeves that you wear over other clothes.
fact: A jacket can also be a cover, like a book jacket, or a jacket potato, which is a potato baked with its skin.
fact: A life jacket is a vest that keeps you floating in water.
fact: «Hi-vis» means bright yellow or orange, so people can be seen easily on roads.
fact: «Waistcoat» means a sleeveless jacket worn over a shirt, so a jacket does not always have sleeves.
exercise: «He put on his jacket because the wind was cold.» What is a jacket here? | A tall building on a hill | A kind of hat | A pocket for keeping a watch in | *A short coat with sleeves, worn over other clothes
exercise: «The book jacket showed a dragon on the front.» What does jacket mean here? | A coat for cold weather | Sleeves for a shirt | *A cover that wraps around something | A dragon's skin
exercise: Ella says a hi-vis jacket is bright so people can see you. Why do people on roads wear hi-vis jackets? | To float in water | To look like a fashion model | To keep their hands warm | *To be seen easily by drivers
test:
«Put on your life jacket before you get in the kayak.» What is a life jacket? | A thick winter coat | *A vest that keeps you floating in water | A cover for a book | A small boat
Ella says a jacket potato is a coat for a potato. What is a jacket potato really? | A potato that is wearing a coat | A potato cooked in a pan with oil | *A potato baked with its skin | A potato cut into chips
exam:
Look at «a waistcoat is a sleeveless jacket worn over a shirt». Which word tells you a waistcoat has no sleeves? | shirt | worn | jacket | *sleeveless
